questions.question_text:
The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{3x(10-x)}{500}$ on $[0,10]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1.2, xmax=11.6, ymin=-0.025, ymax=0.2, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,2,4,6,8,10}, ytick={0.05,0.1,0.15}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:10] {3*x*(10-x)/500};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the mode of $X$.

questions.solution_text:
$f(x)=\frac{3}{500}(10x-x^{2})$
$f'(x)=\frac{3}{500}(10-2x)$
$10-2x=0$
$x=5$
$f''(x)=-\frac{6}{500}<0$, so $x=5$ is a maximum.
$x=5$ lies in $[0,10]$, and $f(0)=f(10)=0$.
The mode is $5$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1.2, xmax=11.6, ymin=-0.025, ymax=0.2, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,2,4,6,8,10}, ytick={0.05,0.1,0.15}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:10] {3*x*(10-x)/500};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:5,0) -- (axis cs:5,0.15);
\node[above] at (axis cs:5,0.16) {mode $=5$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

questions.question_text:
The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{4x^{3}}{81}$ on $[0,3]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.6, xmax=4.2, ymin=-0.18, ymax=1.7, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3}, ytick={0.4,0.8,1.2}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:3] {4*x*x*x/81};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the mode of $X$.

questions.solution_text:
$f'(x)=\frac{12x^{2}}{81}$
$f'(x)>0$ for $0<x\le 3$, so $f$ is increasing across the support.
The only stationary point, $x=0$, gives $f(0)=0$, the smallest value.
$f(3)=\frac{4}{3}$ is the largest value.
The mode is $3$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.6, xmax=4.2, ymin=-0.18, ymax=1.7, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3}, ytick={0.4,0.8,1.2}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:3] {4*x*x*x/81};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:3,0) -- (axis cs:3,1.3333);
\node[above left] at (axis cs:3,1.38) {mode $=3$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

questions.question_text:
The graph shows the probability density function of a continuous random variable $X$ defined on $[0,10]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-0.5,0) -- (7.0,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (5.4,2.5) -- (6,0);
\foreach \x/\lab in {1.2/2,2.4/4,3.6/6,4.8/8,6/10} \node[below] at (\x,0) {$\lab$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the mode of $X$?

questions.solution_text:
The density rises steadily and then falls sharply.
The peak lies one unit to the left of the tick labelled $10$.
The mode is $9$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-0.5,0) -- (7.0,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (5.4,2.5) -- (6,0);
\draw[dashed] (5.4,0) -- (5.4,2.5);
\foreach \x/\lab in {1.2/2,2.4/4,3.6/6,4.8/8,6/10} \node[below] at (\x,0) {$\lab$};
\node[above left] at (5.4,2.5) {mode $=9$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

questions.question_text:
The volume, in litres, of milk a cow yields at one milking is modelled by $X$ with probability density function $f(x)=\frac{3(x-2)(10-x)}{256}$ on $[2,10]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1, xmax=11.6, ymin=-0.03, ymax=0.25, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,2,4,6,8,10}, ytick={0.05,0.1,0.15}]
\addplot[thick, domain=2:10] {3*(x-2)*(10-x)/256};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the most likely yield?

questions.solution_text:
$f(x)=\frac{3}{256}(-x^{2}+12x-20)$
$f'(x)=\frac{3}{256}(-2x+12)$
$-2x+12=0$
$x=6$
$f''(x)=-\frac{6}{256}<0$, so $x=6$ is a maximum.
$x=6$ lies in $[2,10]$, and $f(2)=f(10)=0$.
The most likely yield is $6$ litres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1, xmax=11.6, ymin=-0.03, ymax=0.25, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,2,4,6,8,10}, ytick={0.05,0.1,0.15}]
\addplot[thick, domain=2:10] {3*(x-2)*(10-x)/256};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:6,0) -- (axis cs:6,0.1875);
\node[above] at (axis cs:6,0.2) {mode $=6$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

