The continuous random variable $X$ has probability density function $f(x)=\frac{6x^{2}(5-x)^{2}}{625}$ on $[0,5]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.7, xmax=6.2, ymin=-0.06, ymax=0.5, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5}, ytick={0.1,0.2,0.3}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:5] {6*x*x*(5-x)*(5-x)/625};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the mode of $X$.

questions.solution_text:
$f'(x)=\frac{6}{625}\left(2x(5-x)^{2}-2x^{2}(5-x)\right)$
$=\frac{12}{625}x(5-x)(5-2x)$
$x(5-x)(5-2x)=0$
$x=0$, $x=\frac{5}{2}$ or $x=5$
$f(0)=0$, $f\left(\frac{5}{2}\right)=\frac{3}{8}$ and $f(5)=0$.
The largest value is at $x=\frac{5}{2}$.
The mode is $\frac{5}{2}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.7, xmax=6.2, ymin=-0.06, ymax=0.5, samples=100, clip=false, width=8cm, height=6cm, xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5}, ytick={0.1,0.2,0.3}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:5] {6*x*x*(5-x)*(5-x)/625};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:2.5,0) -- (axis cs:2.5,0.375);
\node[above] at (axis cs:2.5,0.39) {mode $=\frac{5}{2}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

